# Passwords are per card, and optional. A card with none of these set is
# link-only: anyone with the URL can open it.
#
# Precedence (spec v0.2 §14.9), first match wins:
#   CARD_PASSWORD_<SLUG>        this file
#   access.passwordHash         config/cards.config.ts, issued by the editor
#   CARD_PASSWORD               this file
#   none                        link-only
#
# An environment password always wins, so a card set up under v0.1 keeps
# behaving exactly as it did.

# Shared fallback, applied to every card that has no password of its own.
CARD_PASSWORD=
#
# Per-card override: CARD_PASSWORD_<SLUG>, slug upper-cased with every
# non-alphanumeric character replaced by an underscore. For example:
#   /c/2026-newyear-7k2m  ->  CARD_PASSWORD_2026_NEWYEAR_7K2M
#   /c/thanks-sample-3f9q ->  CARD_PASSWORD_THANKS_SAMPLE_3F9Q

# Signs the access cookie for cards whose password is a hash in the config.
# Required as soon as any card has an access.passwordHash: without it, those
# cards stay shut (fail closed) and a production build refuses to start.
# Any long random string will do — `openssl rand -base64 32`.
ACCESS_SECRET=
